# Architecture

_A snapshot of what the codebase IS — regenerated by `/init` and `/compact`, never hand-groomed._

## Stack

Bash (`set -uo pipefail`, macOS/Linux) and Markdown. No compiled language, no package manager. The "runtime" is Claude Code itself: skills orchestrate, agents review, shell scripts do the deterministic work. The implementer runtime is a one-line `config.yaml` swap (`codex` here; `claude` under the `work` profile). The gate declares `shellcheck` as a required tool.

## Layout

- `CLAUDE.md` / `ARCHI.md` / `PLAN.md` — the hot context tier (loaded every session, ~300-line budget).
- `config.yaml` — the single knob: profile, per-role models (incl. `fan_selector`), implementer runtime, `implementer.fan` (best-of-N sample count; default 1 = single-agent), `reviewer.command` (the codex second reviewer, read from `main:config.yaml` at review time — branch config cannot choose the reviewer binary), gate command and required tools, worktree dir.
- `skills/` — the loop stages (`1-plan`…`5-retro`) plus `init`, `compact`, and `docs`. Each is a `SKILL.md`; `1-plan`, `2-implement`, and `docs` carry `prompts/*.tpl` (plan, handoff, followup; docs handoff). `5-retro` closes each unit: four questions, each lesson routed to exactly one of `mechanical`/`contextual`/`process`/`not worth keeping`, applied on a `wt/retro-<slug>` worktree (reused if it already exists; removed after the PR merges) that may touch only `knowledge/`, `PLAN.md`, and the retro file. `2-implement` also documents Fan Mode (N>1): dispatch N samples, gate-filter, adopt a winner. `skills/docs` is the `/docs` documentation-writing stage: it dispatches codex/GPT through the two-arg `agent-exec.sh` to author/rewrite prose, ships by the small-fix path, and runs no gate/no self-review (its handoff fills the footprint from the plan and switches off the AGENTS.md gate rule; the writer summary lands in `work/<slug>/notes.md`). Exposed to Claude Code via the `.claude/skills → ../skills` symlink.
- `.claude/agents/` — fresh-subagent definitions (`plan-reviewer.md`, `code-reviewer.md`, `fan-selector.md`): read-only tools, separate model, cold context.
- `scripts/` — the deterministic layer: `gate.sh` (stack-detecting check runner), `demo.sh` (runs the first sh/bash fence in a plan's `## Demonstration`, respecting headings only outside fences; plain bash from the requested git worktree, streaming output; exit 0 pass or `None:`, 1 block failure or porcelain-status delta, 2 plan/tooling error), `worktree.sh` (isolated-checkout lifecycle: `add` best-effort-fetches and branches new `wt/<slug>` from `origin/main` — HEAD only when no `origin/main` ref exists — then idempotently commits `work/<slug>/plan.md` onto the branch so the plan flows to release; `sync-artifacts` copies top-level regular non-dot primary `work/<slug>/` files, explicitly not symlinks, except `plan.md` into the worktree, then stages the whole `work/<slug>` directory minus `plan.md` so pre-existing worktree-side unit files are also captured, and commits only when staged unit changes exist; the resume path skips the fetch/base change), `agent-exec.sh` (dispatches the implementer into a worktree; normalizes the worktree path to absolute and fails `no new commit` only when the tree was clean before dispatch and a zero-exit dispatch leaves HEAD unchanged *and* the tree still clean — the produced-literally-nothing case), `codex-review.sh` (second-vendor code reviewer: pure reader run from the primary checkout, reads the plan body from the branch via `git show wt/<slug>:…` but `reviewer.command` from `main:config.yaml`, best-effort-fetches then diffs the branch against `origin/main` (falling back to local `main` only when no `refs/remotes/origin/main` ref exists) so a stale local `main` can't pollute the review, pipes plan+diff excluding `work/<slug>` artifacts to the read-only reviewer, captures stdout to a temp file and moves it to `work/<slug>/codex-review.md` only on reviewer exit 0; verdict contract exit 0 = APPROVE / 1 = REQUEST CHANGES / 2 = tooling error, never a verdict), `fan-exec.sh` (best-of-N: `dispatch` spawns N sample worktrees, seeds `work/<slug>/` uncommitted, auto-commits each sample before the gate, prints a manifest of gate-passers; `adopt` retargets `wt/<slug>` to a chosen sample and force-cleans all `<slug>-fan-*` worktrees/branches), `release.sh` (release preconditions incl. the previous unit's non-empty `retro.md` + version/changelog/commit + `work/.last-released` marker on the release branch — the marker must be a regular file byte-identical to `origin/main`'s copy (`cmp`, symlinks refused; on bootstrap with no origin marker, a local marker must be non-empty single-line); never tags, never touches `main`, never pushes; `tag-after-merge` tags post-merge; rollback resets and cleans the marker), `state.sh` (read-only per-work-unit execution-state deriver: given a slug, prints flat `slug`/`stage`/`review`/`next_action` lines derived purely from observable facts — artifact presence under `work/<slug>/`, the whole-line verdict sentinels read from the branch plan via `git show wt/<slug>:…` when the branch exists else the primary plan, the `wt/<slug>` ref, and the `work/.last-released` marker; `review` is `approve` only when both `Code-review verdict: APPROVE` and `Codex-review verdict: APPROVE` are present; seven first-match-wins stage rules `plan→implement→review→release→done`; gate result is deliberately not derived, so `next_action` names `run scripts/gate.sh` live; writes nothing), `archi-fresh.sh` (ref-aware ARCHI freshness check extracted from `release.sh`: `archi-fresh.sh [<ref>]` compares the last-commit epoch of `ARCHI.md` vs `scripts/ skills/ profiles/ config.yaml CLAUDE.md` at `<ref>`, default `HEAD`; strict `<` = stale so equal epochs pass; exit 0 fresh / 1 stale naming the newer paths / 2 missing history; `--help` prints usage. `release.sh check_archi_fresh` delegates to it and `/3-review` runs it against `wt/<slug>` to catch staleness before release). `gate.d/*.sh` are auto-run hooks (`test-scripts.sh` wires the smoke suite in); `gate.d/examples/` contains opt-in hygiene hooks for notebook outputs (`nb-clean.sh`) and data-science artifacts/local paths (`ds-hygiene.sh`).
- `VERSION` / `CHANGELOG.md` — CalVer (`YYYY.M.MICRO`) + Keep-a-Changelog; written only by `release.sh`.
- `profiles/` — `software` (base), `machine-learning` (eval-defines-done + notebook strategy + opt-in repo hygiene hook declaration for data/model artifacts and hardcoded local paths), `database`, `work` (Atlassian/Bitbucket: Claude implementer, Bitbucket CI, Jira reference-only, pointer to ML notebook/repo hygiene because profiles do not merge); selected by `config.yaml`'s `profile:`.
- `tests/test-scripts.sh` — smoke tests for the shell layer: release refusals + a rollback test (pre-commit-hook forced failure; the marker `git clean` insurance path itself is untestable at pre-commit granularity) + the PR-merge flow (bump-on-branch, `origin/main` collision guard, mid-gate re-check, `tag-after-merge` happy + wrong-commit refusal, refusal without either verdict sentinel, the retro refusal matrix + marker integrity cases (deleted/mutated/trailing-newline/symlinked/re-run markers, malformed bootstrap markers) + rollback cases), hermetic fan-exec cases (canned implementer over a real worktree + bare-remote topology), hermetic agent-exec cases (commit / uncommitted / produced-nothing / relative-path / cd-elsewhere / dirty-redispatch dispatches), `worktree.sh add` base/seed cases, `worktree.sh sync-artifacts` artifact-capture/refusal cases, `nb-clean.sh` and `ds-hygiene.sh` example-hook cases, hermetic demo cases (first-block/section scoping, headings inside fences, bash fences, cwd/default dir, plain bash, failure code, dirty-tree refusal, None, missing/empty plan sections, non-git directory, help/arguments), and hermetic codex-review cases (canned reviewer: exit-code matrix with stderr substrings, main-sourced config + ignored branch override, parser termination + commented-command anchor, artifact-only write, worktree stays clean, failed reviewer preserves the prior artifact, missing-plan and wrong-checkout refusals).
- CI: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (GitHub) and `bitbucket-pipelines.yml` (Bitbucket) both run the smoke suite + gate; the `work` profile keeps the Bitbucket one.
- `knowledge/` — cold-tier docs, loaded only on citation (empty but for a README); `work/<slug>/` — one directory per work unit (`plan.md` etc.).
- `AGENTS.md` — the contract the implementer subagent reads; carries a build-discipline ladder (lazy/YAGNI: reuse → stdlib → native → installed dep → one line → minimum code, run after understanding the problem) so the implementer builds the leanest working diff within scope, with explicit validation/security/error-handling boundaries never simplified away.

## Entry points

- **The loop:** `/1-plan` → `/2-implement` → `/3-review` → `/4-release` → `/5-retro`. Invoked as skills from the orchestrator session; full TRIP — release, push, PR, and tag run without an in-session Owner confirm. `/3-review` is dual-vendor: fresh Claude `code-reviewer` subagent + `scripts/codex-review.sh <slug>`, both APPROVE required, both sentinels recorded in one in-place commit on the worktree plan. Both review paths fetch and base the diff on `origin/main` (local-`main` fallback only when no `origin/main` ref exists), so a lagging local `main` cannot pollute the review diff. Both reviewers gate the verdict on severity: only CRITICAL/HIGH findings force `REQUEST CHANGES` (in any round); MEDIUM and LOW never set the verdict — MEDIUM is orchestrator-routed (fix / send back if load-bearing / defer), so a criteria-meeting diff approves without burning the 3-round cap.
- **`scripts/gate.sh`** — run from anywhere in the tree; `cd`s to repo root, auto-detects stacks (Node/Python/Shell/Rust/Go), runs applicable checks + `gate.d/*.sh` hooks. Exit 0 = pass.
- **`scripts/demo.sh <slug> [<dir>]`** — runs the plan demonstration after the implementer gates and commits; the cold code-reviewer re-runs the branch copy and judges whether its output shows the goal. Plans require real inputs and writes only under `mktemp -d`; units with no runnable behavior may use `None: <reason>`.
- **`scripts/release.sh <slug> [--confirm-delta <text>]`** — the release driver; also `check-version` / `next-version` / `tag-after-merge` subcommands. One universal PR-merge topology: fetch-guards `origin/main` (before and after the gate), commits the bump on the release branch, never merges/tags/pushes `main`. After the PR merges, `tag-after-merge <slug>` fetches, verifies `origin/main`'s tip is this release (its `VERSION` and `Release v<version>` subject), and creates the tag locally — the tag push is `/4-release`'s final autonomous step. A release also writes the slug to `work/.last-released` (in the release commit), and `check_previous_retro` refuses the *next* release while `work/<that-slug>/retro.md` is missing or empty, or while the branch's marker is a symlink, deleted, or not byte-identical to `origin/main`'s.
- **`scripts/worktree.sh add|remove|sync-artifacts|list <slug>`** — manages worktrees under `../agentic-coding-worktrees`; `add` bases new branches on `origin/main` and records the unit's `plan.md` onto the branch; `sync-artifacts` records primary-checkout work artifacts on the unit branch without overwriting the worktree plan; **`scripts/agent-exec.sh <worktree> <handoff>`** — feeds a handoff to the implementer runtime inside one.
- **`scripts/state.sh <slug>`** — prints the work unit's derived execution state (`stage`/`review`/`next_action`) so a cold session learns where a unit stands and what comes next without the prior conversation; read-only, gate result out of scope by design.
- **`scripts/fan-exec.sh dispatch <slug> <handoff> <N>` / `adopt <slug> <sample-branch>`** — the best-of-N primitive behind `2-implement`'s Fan Mode; sequential (N× wall-clock), activated only when `implementer.fan > 1`.

## Conventions

- **Writer never reviews.** Reviews come only from fresh `.claude/agents/` subagents (read-only, separate model). Never review a diff produced in your own thread.
- **The gate and release are scripts, and authoritative.** Never overrule `gate.sh` or `release.sh`; enforcement never lives in skill prose.
- **Implementation happens in worktrees, never in this checkout.** Use `worktree.sh`.
- **Verdict sentinels are distinct by stage and vendor:** `Plan verdict:`, `Code-review verdict:`, `Codex-review verdict:`; `release.sh` releases only on exact `Code-review verdict: APPROVE` **and** `Codex-review verdict: APPROVE` lines in the branch's plan. Exit ≥2 from `codex-review.sh` is a tooling error, never a verdict — no sentinel may be recorded from artifact prose after a non-zero exit.
- **Release preconditions** (all before anything irreversible; trap rollback after): APPROVE sentinel, gate green, `ARCHI.md` fresher than the last commit touching `scripts/ skills/ profiles/ config.yaml CLAUDE.md` (via `scripts/archi-fresh.sh`; `/3-review` runs the same check earlier and heals staleness with a targeted branch edit, so release rarely trips it), version strictly increasing, and `origin/main` an ancestor of the release branch — re-checked after the gate to close the cross-release version collision.
- **`worktree.sh` only asks git** (`git worktree`, `git rev-parse`), never inspects `.git` directly — works from inside a worktree where `.git` is a file. Preserve this. **YAML parsing is naive awk** in `gate.sh`/`worktree.sh`/`agent-exec.sh`/`release.sh`; `gate.sh` is section-scoped, not depth-aware; replace with `yq` only if it bites.
- All shell scripts must pass `shellcheck` (enforced by the gate). Use `set -uo pipefail`.
- Vendor/model names live only in `config.yaml`. Reviewer models are additionally in agent frontmatter, which is authoritative; config.yaml documents intent.

## Verification

`bash scripts/gate.sh` — required-tool preflight, shellcheck over all tracked `*.sh`, plus the `gate.d/` hook running `tests/test-scripts.sh` (200 checks, incl. the gate tool-preflight cases, the PR-merge release flow + `tag-after-merge`, the marker-integrity matrix, the dual-sentinel refusals, the hermetic fan-exec, agent-exec, codex-review, and demo suites (section/fence scoping, cwd, plain bash, exit-code matrix and dirty-tree refusal), the `worktree.sh add` base/seed cases, the `worktree.sh sync-artifacts` artifact-capture cases, and the `nb-clean.sh` / `ds-hygiene.sh` example-hook cases). CI runs the gate on push. Currently green.
#!/usr/bin/env bash
# The gate. Exit 0 = pass. Non-zero = fail, and everything printed is the
# feedback the implementer gets. Agents do not overrule this script.
#
# Auto-detects the stacks present and runs every applicable check.
# Profile- or project-specific checks go in scripts/gate.d/*.sh (run last).
set -uo pipefail

cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)" || exit 1

fail=0
fail_message() {
  echo "GATE: FAIL — fix everything marked ✗ above."
}

run() {
  echo "▶ $*"
  if ! "$@"; then
    fail=1
    echo "✗ FAILED: $*"
  fi
}

required_tools=
if [[ ${GATE_REQUIRED_TOOLS+set} ]]; then
  required_tools=$GATE_REQUIRED_TOOLS
elif [[ -f config.yaml ]]; then
  required_tools=$(awk '
    /^[^[:space:]#][^:]*:/ {
      f = ($0 ~ /^gate:[[:space:]]*($|#)/)
      next
    }
    f && /^[[:space:]]*required_tools:/ {
      sub(/^[[:space:]]*required_tools:[[:space:]]*/, "")
      sub(/[[:space:]]+#.*$/, "")
      gsub(/^[[:space:]]+|[[:space:]]+$/, "")
      if (($0 ~ /^".*"$/) || ($0 ~ /^'\''.*'\''$/)) {
        sub(/^["'\'']/, "")
        sub(/["'\'']$/, "")
      }
      print
      exit
    }
  ' config.yaml)
fi

missing_required=()
if [[ -n "$required_tools" ]]; then
  IFS=: read -r -a required_tool_list <<<"$required_tools"
  for tool in "${required_tool_list[@]}"; do
    [[ -z "$tool" ]] && continue
    if ! command -v "$tool" >/dev/null; then
      missing_required+=("$tool")
    fi
  done
fi

if [[ ${#missing_required[@]} -gt 0 ]]; then
  for tool in "${missing_required[@]}"; do
    echo "✗ missing required tool: $tool"
  done
  fail_message
  exit 1
fi

skip() {
  echo "⊘ skipped: $1 (not installed)"
}

# --- Node ---------------------------------------------------------------
if [[ -f package.json ]]; then
  if command -v node >/dev/null; then
    typecheck_script=0
    for s in lint typecheck test; do
      if node -e "process.exit(require('./package.json').scripts?.['$s'] ? 0 : 1)" 2>/dev/null; then
        run npm run --silent "$s"
        [[ "$s" == typecheck ]] && typecheck_script=1
      fi
    done
    # No typecheck script but a TypeScript project: let the compiler judge.
    if [[ $typecheck_script -eq 0 && -f tsconfig.json ]]; then
      if npx --no-install tsc --version >/dev/null 2>&1; then
        run npx --no-install tsc --noEmit
      else
        skip tsc
      fi
    fi
  else
    skip node
  fi
fi

# --- Python -------------------------------------------------------------
if [[ -f pyproject.toml || -f setup.py || -f requirements.txt ]]; then
  if command -v ruff >/dev/null; then
    run ruff check .
  else
    skip ruff
  fi
  if compgen -G "tests/*" >/dev/null; then
    if command -v pytest >/dev/null; then
      run pytest -q
    else
      skip pytest
    fi
  fi
fi

# --- Shell --------------------------------------------------------------
shell_files=()
while IFS= read -r f; do shell_files+=("$f"); done \
  < <(git ls-files '*.sh' 2>/dev/null)
if [[ ${#shell_files[@]} -gt 0 ]]; then
  if command -v shellcheck >/dev/null; then
    run shellcheck "${shell_files[@]}"
  else
    skip shellcheck
  fi
fi

# --- Rust / Go ----------------------------------------------------------
if [[ -f Cargo.toml ]]; then
  if command -v cargo >/dev/null; then
    run cargo clippy -q -- -D warnings
    run cargo test -q
  else
    skip cargo
  fi
fi
if [[ -f go.mod ]]; then
  if command -v go >/dev/null; then
    run go vet ./...
    run go test ./...
  else
    skip go
  fi
fi

# --- Profile / project extensions ---------------------------------------
for hook in scripts/gate.d/*.sh; do
  [[ -f "$hook" ]] && run bash "$hook"
done

if [[ $fail -eq 0 ]]; then
  echo "GATE: PASS"
else
  fail_message
fi
exit $fail
