# Architecture

_Generated and maintained by `/init` and `/compact` — a snapshot of what the codebase IS, so agents don't re-derive it every session. Regenerate rather than hand-groom._

## Stack

_Languages, frameworks, key dependencies._

## Layout

_Top-level directories and what lives in each._

## Entry points

_How the thing runs: main binaries, servers, CLIs, notebooks._

## Conventions

_Only the ones an agent would get wrong by guessing: naming, error handling, test placement, anything idiosyncratic._

## Verification

_The commands that prove the code works. `scripts/gate.sh` wraps these._
# Plan

One screen, always. Reasoning lives in work units — link, don't restate.

## Objective

_What this project is trying to be. One paragraph max._

## Now

_The active work unit(s), one line each: `work/<slug>` — what and why._

## Decisions

_One line each, newest first: date — decision — link to work unit or commit._

## Risks

_Top 3 at most. If a risk isn't shaping current decisions, it doesn't belong here._

